# Template for the on-demand E2E harness (test/e2e/**, `npm run test:e2e`).
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in real values — `.env.local` is
# gitignored and read by test/e2e/global-setup.ts before the suite runs.
#
# IMPORTANT — never add a VITE_ prefix to any variable below, and never add
# one to a variable that plays the same role in the future. Vite inlines
# every VITE_-prefixed variable into the client bundle at build time, and
# that bundle ships inside CouchDB's share/www — a VITE_ git token would be
# readable by anyone who opens the app's dev tools. These variables are read
# only by test/e2e/global-setup.ts, in plain Node, and must stay unprefixed
# so Vite never touches them.
#
# With nothing set, `npm run test:e2e` SKIPS visibly (not silently) and
# prints which variable is missing. `npm test` never reads this file at all.

# --- GitHub (Enterprise) -----------------------------------------------
# A personal access token with repo write access to CCA_E2E_GIT_REPO below.
# Never commit a real value. The harness installs a leak guard that throws
# if this string ever reaches a log line.
CCA_E2E_GIT_TOKEN=

# The repository the E2E suite is allowed to write to. It must NOT be a
# repository anyone depends on: the suite creates a throwaway branch
# (e2e/<runId>) off the default branch, commits under a per-run path
# prefix, and deletes the branch afterwards — but it does perform real
# commits while the run is in progress.
CCA_E2E_GIT_REPO=https://github.example.com/owner/repo

# GitHub Enterprise host (no path), e.g. https://github.example.com.
# Leave empty to target github.com.
CCA_E2E_GIT_BASE_URL=

# --- CouchDB -------------------------------------------------------------
# Base URL of the CouchDB the suite authenticates against. Any userinfo
# (user:pass@) is stripped before use — Node's fetch refuses to construct a
# request from a URL that embeds credentials. Put the account in
# CCA_E2E_ADMIN_USER/PASSWORD instead (see the auth section below).
CCA_E2E_COUCH_URL=http://localhost:5984

# --- Auth: how the harness authenticates against CouchDB ------------------
# "jwt" (default) or "basic".
#
# CouchDB has three authentication handlers — jwt, cookie, and default
# (Basic). The cookie one is unusable here: "credentials: include" is a
# browser mechanism and is inert under Node's fetch (no cookie jar), so a
# request after a successful POST /_session still 401s. That leaves jwt and
# basic, and ApiClient can now send either (setToken / setCredential).
#
#   jwt   — obtains a token for an admin user via a Keycloak password grant
#           and hands it to apiClient.setToken(). Needs CouchDB's [jwt_keys]
#           wired to that realm, which the devcontainer does
#           (scripts/seed-dev.sh). This is the same Bearer path the product
#           uses in production, not a test-only shortcut.
#
#   basic — skips Keycloak entirely and sends Authorization: Basic. Use this
#           for any CouchDB WITHOUT an IdP configured, which is most of them.
#           CCA_E2E_ADMIN_USER and CCA_E2E_ADMIN_PASSWORD must then be set
#           explicitly — they are CouchDB credentials in this mode, not
#           Keycloak ones, so the devcontainer defaults below do NOT apply
#           and the suite SKIPS (visibly) if either is missing.
#
# CCA_E2E_AUTH_MODE=jwt

# The five below default to the devcontainer's own seeded values, so most
# jwt-mode runs need none of them. Override when pointing at a different
# Keycloak/CouchDB pairing — or, in basic mode, set the last two to a
# CouchDB server-admin account.
# CCA_E2E_KEYCLOAK_URL=http://localhost:8080
# CCA_E2E_KEYCLOAK_REALM=couch
# CCA_E2E_KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_ID=couch-companion-ui
# CCA_E2E_ADMIN_USER=hariseldon
# CCA_E2E_ADMIN_PASSWORD=password
#
# Known quirk (jwt mode only): CouchDB sets userCtx.name to the JWT's `sub`
# claim (a Keycloak UUID), not to "hariseldon" — expected, not a bug in the
# harness. In basic mode userCtx.name is the real account name.

# --- SPA mode gate (scripts/spa-check.mjs, `npm run test:spa`) ------------
# A separate harness from the E2E suite above, with its own variables: it
# needs a real browser and a real CouchDB on a real *different origin*,
# because SPA mode (spec D5) is where CORS preflights, cross-site cookies
# and the page CSP actually apply — and none of those exist under happy-dom
# or Node's fetch. See issue #37.
#
# With nothing set it SKIPS visibly and exits 0, so `npm test` and
# scripts/check.sh stay hermetic.
#
# The account below is a COUCHDB account (it is posted to /_session and used
# to read `[cors]` config), and must be a server admin. It is deliberately
# NOT defaulted from CCA_E2E_ADMIN_USER/PASSWORD, which in the E2E suite's
# default jwt mode are Keycloak credentials — sending those to CouchDB would
# fail in a way that reads like a bug in the gate.
CCA_SPA_COUCH_URL=http://localhost:5984
CCA_SPA_USER=
CCA_SPA_PASSWORD=

# Port the harness serves the app on. Fixed rather than free-chosen, because
# CouchDB's `[cors] origins` has to name the origin. The gate serves the same
# build from BOTH `http://localhost:<port>` (same site as a CouchDB on
# localhost — cookies ignore ports, CORS does not) and
# `http://127.0.0.1:<port>` (a different site), so both need allowing:
#
#   curl -X PUT $CCA_SPA_COUCH_URL/_node/_local/_config/cors/origins \
#        -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
#        -d '"http://localhost:5173, http://127.0.0.1:5173"'
#
# `[chttpd] enable_cors` and `[cors] credentials` must both be "true". The
# gate reads all three and says exactly what to set if they are not; it never
# writes CouchDB config itself.
# CCA_SPA_APP_PORT=5173
#
# Note on `[couch_httpd_auth] same_site`: over plain HTTP, leave it UNSET.
# CouchDB only adds `Secure` to the session cookie when the request arrived on
# a TLS socket (X-Forwarded-Ssl/-Proto do not change this), so `same_site =
# none` on an http:// server emits `SameSite=None` WITHOUT `Secure`, which
# Chrome refuses outright (`SameSiteNoneInsecure`) — breaking not just the
# cross-site login it was meant to fix but the same-site one that worked
# before. Verified with this gate against CouchDB 3.5.2.
